# A CONSUMER MUST BE ABLE TO READ THE NAME THE CONTRACT GIVES IT.
#
# apply_governance granted on entity.tables() alone -- the physical _rev<N> names -- so
# the unversioned VIEW that the data contract, the DBML diagram and the source-to-target
# mapping all tell a consumer to bind to carried NO GRANT AT ALL. The views existed and
# nobody could select from them; Adrian found it in the catalog explorer, where the whole
# raw_vault schema showed five tables and no views.
#
# That made the versioning mechanism decorative: the one name that survives a cutover was
# the one name nobody could read. Both names are granted now (Adrian's decision), and the
# view only where it exists -- the same activity condition the quarantine twin already
# used, because a grant against an object that does not exist fails the run.
_ag_spec = _ilu2.spec_from_file_location("ag_grants", ROOT / "checks" / "apply_governance.py")
