# DEF-54: found by the FIRST REAL LOAD, not by any test. An inferred streaming table's
# column order is the union of its FLOWS -- the ghost flow leads with hk and the system
# columns, so hashdiff lands ninth -- while the loader SELECTs in _projection order, where
# hashdiff is second. The positional INSERT put a BINARY hashdiff into a TIMESTAMP
# load_dts and failed with DATATYPE_MISMATCH. A whole-branch reviewer had warned that "an
# INSERT that relies on positional matching is fragile if anything reorders"; the fix wave
# added an explicit SELECT list and left the INSERT positional, which is half the fix.
print("\n== DEF-54: the INSERT names its target columns ==")

