# THE SYNTHETIC PARTNER, and it carries the behaviour. The check above is fix-safe -- it
# stays green the day both markers are removed for the right reason -- which is exactly
# when it stops asserting anything. This one labels the REAL workbook's rows against a
# mapping written here, so it keeps proving the three-way split whatever the real mapping
# says. Customer_Invoice_ID's one row is "All CSVs", so a marked field must come back as
# FOUR unresolved columns, not one.
